# Copy to .env.local.
#
# There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable in this app, deliberately. Everything here
# is a server secret, and a Firebase credential compiled into a browser bundle
# is not recoverable by rotating a key later. See src/lib/firestore.ts.

# --- Firestore ------------------------------------------------------------
# Set → the local emulator, no credentials needed. Unset → the real project,
# and then GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS is mandatory. Exactly the rule
# scripts/src/lib/firestore.ts and apps/console use, so the three cannot drift.
FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=localhost:8080
GCLOUD_PROJECT=kgc-conference-app-and-website

# Only when FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST is unset.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/serviceAccount.json

# --- Order confirmation links --------------------------------------------
# Signs the capability token in /order/{token}. Required: the confirmation page
# shows a claim code, and the registration id it would otherwise be keyed by is
# derived from the email address and therefore guessable. Any random string of
# 16+ characters; rotating it invalidates outstanding confirmation links.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
WEB_ORDER_SECRET=change-me-openssl-rand-base64-32

# --- Stripe (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Leave both unset and the site falls back to a clearly labelled test purchase
# that writes the same registration and states on screen that no payment was
# taken. Set them and the site uses hosted Stripe Checkout.
#
# Use a test key (sk_test_…) for anything that is not the real conference.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
#
# From `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3200/api/stripe/webhook`, or from
# the endpoint's page in the Stripe dashboard.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# --- Email (Resend) -------------------------------------------------------
# Leave RESEND_API_KEY unset and no transactional email is sent. That is a
# supported state, not a broken one: every attempt is still written to the
# `emailLog` collection with status `skipped`, so the dashboard shows plainly
# that nothing went out rather than implying it did.
#
# Get the key at https://resend.com/api-keys (starts `re_`).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# MUST be a domain verified at https://resend.com/domains, or every send is
# rejected with 403. A friendly name matters more than it looks — "KGC 2027" is
# recognised in an inbox list and a bare address is not.
# EMAIL_FROM=KGC 2027 <tickets@knowledgegraph.tech>
#
# Where "just reply to this email" lands. Defaults to hello@knowledgegraph.tech.
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=hello@knowledgegraph.tech

# --- Deployment -----------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed behind a proxy that rewrites Host, or when Stripe's return URL
# must be an absolute public origin. Derived from the request otherwise.
# WEB_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://www.knowledgegraph.tech

# --- Demo mode ------------------------------------------------------------
# `1` makes the pay button approve the purchase without a payment processor,
# shows a cosmetic card box, and prints the buyer's details in a panel at the
# bottom of the checkout page. The order is written as `paid` and tagged
# `channel: 'demo'`. Never set this alongside a real STRIPE_SECRET_KEY.
# DEMO_MODE=1
